Short strings reproduced for interoperability

The source contains short byte sequences used to locate exact positions within a
specific build, including the list of locale identifiers the application offers
in its language picker. Locale identifiers are factual interface data required to
perform the replacement, not creative content. The localized display name
"简体中文" is the CLDR endonym for the zh-Hans locale.

The three sha256 digests recorded in src/claude_zh_patch/compat.py are
fingerprints used to refuse unexpected builds. They are not content.
